      "writtenOn": "2023-03-06T14:42:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Refer to the original `AuthPerOperation` test, it seems that KM expects `HAT \u003e challenge` identify to the `handle_`.\nSo that assign an arbitrary challenge causes the HAT validation fail in strongbox.\nIs it expected?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 391,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 391,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "70876a596c87c528ea1a3cc2b8d7a3e878ccd233",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a2727a2_67dcc911",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/vts/functional/AuthTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 391,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-06T16:02:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My rough understanding of the `AUTH_TIMEOUT(3)` tag was that it allowed use of the key as long as the relevant user had authenticated within the last 3 seconds -- and because that\u0027s prior to the `begin()`, there isn\u0027t a need to check the challenge.\n\nBut then a StrongBox device without a clock makes that more complicated, because the device can\u0027t tell if the auth token is in the last 3 seconds or not.  For that case, the subsequent `update`/`finish` gets a `TimestampToken` that does have the challenge from `begin`, so now StrongBox knows the time and can check it.\n\nDo you think that the HAT should have the challenge value from the `begin()` call (which would mean the authentication has to happen after the `begin`) ?",
      "parentUuid": "f10f228e_181cc535",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 391,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 391,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "70876a596c87c528ea1a3cc2b8d7a3e878ccd233",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a2f0534_9b275dc3",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/vts/functional/AuthTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 391,
      "author": {
        "id": 1043663
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-06T19:02:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "David is correct. For timeout-bound keys KeyMint should not pay any attention the challenge in the HAT.  If the KeyMint needs a `TimestampToken` that token must have the challenge from `begin()` in it.",
      "parentUuid": "3a2727a2_67dcc911",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 391,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 391,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "70876a596c87c528ea1a3cc2b8d7a3e878ccd233",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1549230f_c541e2ce",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/vts/functional/AuthTest.cpp",
