      "writtenOn": "2023-03-06T14:42:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Double check the strongbox implementation, since \n`TAG_USER_AUTH_TYPE \u003d HardwareAuthenticatorType::NONE` when generateKey(), it won\u0027t take effect on the further HAT validation (`HAT \u003e authenticatorType`).\nAnd because the time_token has valid timestamp \u0026 sid, strongbox will just return OK here.\n\nIt seems that the meaning of `HardwareAuthenticatorType::NONE` is similar to `NO_AUTH_REQUIRED`.\nIs my understanding correct?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 411,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 411,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "70876a596c87c528ea1a3cc2b8d7a3e878ccd233",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dad2eec0_eeef256a",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/vts/functional/AuthTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 411,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-06T16:02:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I *think* that setting `AUTH_TYPE\u003dHardwareAuthenticatorType::NONE` basically produces an unusable key -- it requires authentication for use, but it allows for no valid authenticators.  (`HardwareAuthenticatorType::ANY` would instead allow use of any authenticator type.)\n\nBut I had previously guessed otherwise, so I\u0027m not completely sure.",
      "parentUuid": "1549230f_c541e2ce",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 411,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 411,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "70876a596c87c528ea1a3cc2b8d7a3e878ccd233",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
